WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.800
In this video, you open a virtual machine in SUSE Observability and follow its relations to its host, storage, and network in the Topology perspective.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.460
Open the main menu.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.880
Expand SUSE Virtualization.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.930
Select Virtual machines.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:31.810
The view lists the VMs of every connected cluster. Open the VM named kasm, which runs on the far-edge cluster.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:42.580
Highlights opens first. The About card shows the VM's status, host, IP address, vCPUs, memory, and guest operating system.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:52.370
Related resources lists what the VM uses, such as its VM network, its disks, the Longhorn volume, and the virt-launcher pod.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:01:19.430
Select Topology to draw these relations as a map.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:30.263
Each virtual machine is a component with relations to its host, storage, and network. Next, you investigate an unhealthy virtual machine.
